  "content": {
    "id": "v2-7aed5b-p9-practice-slot-2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Each student multiplies both sides by the denominator and keeps the inequality sign. Find the correct solution.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "v2-7aed5b-p9-practice-slot-2-slot-2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{5}{x+2}<1$, the student obtains $x>3$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<-2$ or $x>3$.",
          "worked": "The student's multiplier $x+2$ is negative for $x<-2$. For $x\\ne-2$, multiply by $(x+2)^2>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}5(x+2)&<(x+2)^2\\\\0&<(x+2)(x+2-5)\\\\(x+2)(x-3)&>0\\end{align*}$$\nThe quadratic is positive outside its roots, so $x<-2$ or $x>3$. The restriction $x\\ne-2$ is already satisfied.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-7aed5b-p9-practice-slot-2-slot-2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{4}{x-3}\\le2$, the student obtains $x\\ge5$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<3$ or $x\\ge5$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne3$, multiply by $(x-3)^2>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}4(x-3)&\\le2(x-3)^2\\\\0&\\le2(x-3)(x-3-2)\\\\(x-3)(x-5)&\\ge0\\end{align*}$$\nThe quadratic is non-negative outside its roots, including the roots: $x\\le3$ or $x\\ge5$. Exclude $x=3$ because the denominator is zero.\nTherefore $x<3$ or $x\\ge5$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      }
    ]
  },
